= Smartwire

If you have a DSMR 5 energy meter, you do not need an SMA emeter.
Measurement data can be read from the P1 port and converted to the
Speedwire format expected by SMA devices. An ESP microcontroller can
do this.

This project started with a Smartstuff Ethernet P1 Dongle Pro+, an
esp32c3 with a WIZnet W5500 ethernet controller. There are, however,
many similar devices that can easily be made to work as well.


== Disclaimer

This project is not endorsed by SMA and the software comes with no
warranty. The mapping from P1 telegrams to Speedwire telegrams is not
exact. Moreover, some DSMR 5 meters are known to produce measurement
data at insufficient frequency for correct use by SMA devices.


== Usage

Attach the dongle via USB and run `cargo run --release --features p1ep`.


== Code organization

`board::p1ep`: Peripheral configuration specific to the Smartstuff dongle.

`cosem`: Type definitions from IEC 62056 and a trait for data sources.

`crc`: Implementation of the CRC checksum as used in the DSMR protocol.

`emeter`: Producer of Speedwire telegrams from an IEC 62056 data source.

`line_reader`: Buffered line-based reading from a source of bytes.

`number_reader`: Stream-based parsing of decimal numerals.

`p1`: Consumer of P1 telegrams and provider of an IEC 62056 data source.


